  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAAF Core Contribution 2023-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Safe Abortion Action Fund (SAAF)  is multi-donor fund supporting grassroot civil society organisations advocating for the right to safe abortion and improved SRHR on different levels. The subgrants focus on safe abortions and access to reproductive health care, including family planning. Young girls and women with disabilities are at a great disadvantage when it comes to matters of sexuality and abortion. Due to the intersectionality of their gender and their disability, girls and women with disabilities can find themselves unable to make decisions about their own bodies. SAAF embeds the perspective of intersectionality and includes girls and women living with disabilities among their target groups.

Supported organisations are found in the following countries: Bangladesh, Cambodia, India, Indonesia, Nepal, Thailand, Benin, Burkina Faso, Burundi, Cameroon, Congo, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Ghana, Guinea, Kenya, Liberia, Madagascar, Malawi, Mozambique, Nigeria, Rwanda, Sao Tome, Sierra Leone, South Africa, Tanzania, Uganda, Zambia, Zimbabwe, Argentina, Bolivia, Brazil, Colombia, Ecuador, El Salvador, Domonican republic, Guatemala, Haiti, Jamaica, Mexico, Nicaragua, Paraguay, Peru, Iraq, Lebanon, Morocco, Bosnia, Moldova , Tajikistan, Kyrgyzstan, and Turkey.</narrative>
  </description>
